# PortSwigger Web Security Academy

## Server-side prototype pollution

### Objective

The objective of this lab was to exploit a **server-side prototype pollution vulnerability** in the `/my-account/change-address` endpoint and use it to escalate the privileges of the authenticated user.

The vulnerable functionality accepted JSON input and recursively merged user-controlled properties into an object. By abusing the `constructor.prototype` property, it was possible to modify `Object.prototype` on the server.

The final exploitation chain was:

```text
User-controlled JSON
        ↓
constructor.prototype
        ↓
Object.prototype pollution
        ↓
isAdmin = true
        ↓
Privilege escalation
        ↓
Access to /admin
        ↓
Delete user "carlos"
```

---

