# Reconnaissance

After authenticating to the application, I accessed the account page and submitted a change to the billing/delivery address.

Using **Burp Suite → Proxy → HTTP history**, I identified the following request:

```http
POST /my-account/change-address HTTP/2
Host: 0a9400520451829b813b66e300e600a0.web-security-academy.net
Cookie: session=KQEAa8G1EyE0ny3wwO1UrfgK37cSlqiB
Content-Type: application/json;charset=UTF-8

{
  "address_line_1": "Wiener HQ",
  "address_line_2": "One Wiener Way",
  "city": "Tarragona",
  "postcode": "BU1 1RP",
  "country": "UK",
  "sessionId": "KQEAa8G1EyE0ny3wwO1UrfgK37cSlqiB"
}
```

The server returned the updated user object:

```json
{
  "username": "wiener",
  "firstname": "Peter",
  "lastname": "Wiener",
  "address_line_1": "Wiener HQ",
